#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
swg-sub — the public subscription surface.

A tiny, READ-ONLY companion to swg-panel-server. It runs on the panel host and
serves one thing: a per-user shareable page of that user's WireGuard/AmneziaWG
QRs + configs, reached at

    https://sub.<domain>/<token>#<unlock-key>

The <token> (URL path) is an opaque per-user id — the server sees it and uses it
only to find which ciphertext bucket to serve. The <unlock-key> lives in the URL
*fragment*, which browsers never send to any server, so this process can NEVER
decrypt a peer's private key: it only ever serves ciphertext + non-secret params.
The browser on the phone does the decrypt with the fragment key.

By design this program has ZERO write, admin, or node code. It reads only the
subset of state it needs (roster, nodes, per-node snapshots, the subs token map +
blobs, and a tiny subs/serve.json), all read-only. It never reads the secrets that
would let a compromise escalate — the login hash, the TLS key, the subscription-key
vault, panel-settings (webhook secrets) — which is why it runs as its OWN
unprivileged user and the installer masks those paths from it. A compromise of this
internet-facing surface yields only ciphertext, never the fleet.

Least privilege: bare-metal runs it as user `swgsub` (group swg, read-only) with the
secret paths made InaccessiblePaths in the unit; docker runs it as a separate
container with the state mounted :ro and the same secrets masked (/dev/null + tmpfs).
The files it DOES read are group-readable (0640); the vault + login hash stay 0600.

Config all happens in the panel: Settings → Subscriptions (master enable, base URL,
this listener's host/port/TLS). SWG_SUB_FLEET (defaults to the panel's
/etc/swg-panel/fleet.json) locates the state files; enable + host/port/TLS are read
from subs/serve.json (which the panel mirrors from its settings) — NOT from
panel-settings.json, so this surface never opens the file that holds webhook secrets.
The bind is set once at startup; the master `subscriptions.enabled` flag is re-read on
EVERY request, so toggling it in the panel takes effect immediately — off ⇒ 404.
"""

